OL,3,GNEWSACouncil backs exploring asylum
OL,4,Ahousing referendum
OL,5,
OL,6,FPhilip Faircloth-Mutton, a Reform UK
OL,7,Fcouncillor and deputy leader of the
OL,8,Fauthority, put forward the motion as he
OL,9,Fsaid communities should have a say over
OL,10,FHome Office plans to convert RAF
OL,11,FBarnham into accommodation for asylum
OL,12,Fseekers.
OL,14,FOpposition councillors said a
OL,15,Freferendum could cost up to #2m to
OL,16,Fhold, would not be legally binding and
OL,17,Fwould come too late to change policy if
OL,18,Fit was run in May.
